From a39e1c9486a6dc2060d8d1adb8a917f44e726aa4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ashish Chauhan <ashish.chauhan@imgtec.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 13:57:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 05/24] pvr: program DOUTI count from the fragment shader
 inputs

The number of DOUTI commands was taken from the vertex shader's output
range. The iterators feed the fragment shader, so the count should follow
the coefficients the fragment shader consumes instead.

The two differ when a vertex output isn't read by the fragment shader.
Transform feedback makes that common, since a varying can be captured
without being iterated, and transform feedback tests fail without this.

Signed-off-by: Ashish Chauhan <ashish.chauhan@imgtec.com>
Reviewed-by: Simon Perretta <simon.perretta@imgtec.com>
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/44385>
(cherry picked from commit 03fd7d3424165a7feb27c1950935273ab663fa4e)
---
 src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_pipeline.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_pipeline.c b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_pipeline.c
index 2564e59c..aa63eb45 100644
--- a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_pipeline.c
+++ b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_arch_pipeline.c
@@ -1724,7 +1724,7 @@ static void pvr_graphics_pipeline_setup_fragment_coeff_program(
                       "amend nir var linking.");
       }
 
-      unsigned count = vtxout_range->count;
+      unsigned count = cf_range->count / ROGUE_USC_COEFFICIENT_SET_SIZE;
 
       unsigned vtxout = vtxout_range->start;
 
